328	170,1495,630,2035	328. Common Flax.	A leafy sprig of Common Flax with narrow pointed leaves, one open flower of five broad veined petals round its stamens, and a closed bud above.
329	683,1575,1402,2030	329. Half of a flower, enlarged.	A Flax flower cut in half and enlarged: three spreading veined petals, the stamens with their bases joined, and five styles above the small ovary with its seeds.
330	1458,1790,1635,2008	330. Pod, cut across.	The round Flax pod cut across, showing ten cells arranged like the spokes of a wheel, each holding a seed.
